e your own free Google Maps API key.'=>'to create your own free Google Maps API key.','You are using The Events Calendar\'s built-in Google Maps API key.'=>'You are using The Events Calendar\'s built-in Google Maps API key.','If you do not add your own API key, the built-in API key will always populate this field and some map-related functionality will be limited '=>'If you do not add your own API key, the built-in API key will always populate this field and some map-related functionality will be limited ','<p>The Events Calendar comes with an API key for basic maps functionality. If you’d like to use more advanced features like custom map pins or dynamic map loads, you’ll need to get your own %1$sGoogle Maps API key</a>. %2$sRead More</a>.</p>'=>'<p>The Events Calendar comes with an API key for basic maps functionality. If you’d like to use more advanced features like custom map pins or dynamic map loads, you’ll need to get your own %1$sGoogle Maps API key</a>. %2$sRead more</a>.</p>','to learn more about using it with The Events Calendar'=>'to learn more about using it with The Events Calendar','You are using a custom Google Maps API key.'=>'You are using a custom Google Maps API key.','Cron-based'=>'Cron-based','Asynchronous'=>'Asynchronous','Unsupported'=>'Unsupported','Successfully stopped and cleared 1 asynchronous queue process.'=>'Successfully stopped and cleared 1 asynchronous queue process.' . "\0" . 'Successfully stopped and cleared %d asynchronous queue processes.','No asynchronous queue processes to clear.'=>'No asynchronous queue processes to clear.','The event tag ID or name'=>'The event tag ID or name','The event category ID or name'=>'The event category ID or name','Events should be filtered by their post_parent being the specified one.'=>'Events should be filtered by their post_parent being the specified one.','Include events with one of the post IDs specified in the array of CSV list, date filters will be ignored.'=>'Include events with one of the post IDs specified in the array of CSV list, date filters will be ignored.','Unable to process this import - a breakage or conflict may have resulted in the import halting.'=>'Unable to process this import - a breakage or conflict may have resulted in the import halting.','Calendar of %s'=>'Calendar of %s','%s Views Navigation'=>'%s Views Navigation','%s Search and Views Navigation'=>'%s Search and Views Navigation','If you have extended our plugin(s) to send data to a third-party service such as Eventbrite, Google Maps, or PayPal, user information may be passed to these external services. These services may be located abroad.'=>'If you have extended our plugin(s) to send data to a third-party service such as Eventbrite, Google Maps, or PayPal, user information may be passed to these external services. These services may be located abroad.','Where We Send Your Data'=>'Where We Send Your Data','Certain data may be exported or removed upon users’ requests via the existing Exporter or Eraser. Please note, however, that several “edge cases” exist in which we are unable to perfect the gathering and export of all data for your end users. We suggest running a search in your local database, as well as within the WordPress Dashboard, in order to identify all data collected and stored for your specific user requests.'=>'Certain data may be exported or removed upon users’ requests via the existing Exporter or Eraser. Please note, however, that several “edge cases” exist in which we are unable to perfect the gathering and export of all data for your end users. We suggest running a search in your local database, as well as within the WordPress Dashboard, in order to identify all data collected and stored for your specific user requests.','All information (data) is retained in the local database indefinitely, unless otherwise deleted.'=>'All information (data) is retained in the local database indefinitely, unless otherwise deleted.','How Long You Retain this Data'=>'How Long You Retain this Data','We make use of certain APIs, in order to provide specific features.'=>'We make use of certain APIs, in order to provide specific features.','The Events Calendar suite offers the use of third-party API keys. The primary functions are to enhance the features we\'ve built in, some of which use Google Maps, PayPal, Eventbrite, and Meetup. These API keys are not supplied by The Events Calendar.'=>'The Events Calendar suite offers the use of third-party API keys. The primary functions are to enhance the features we\'ve built in, some of which use Google Maps, PayPal, Eventbrite, and Meetup. These API keys are not supplied by The Events Calendar.','API Keys'=>'API Keys','When purchasing Eventbrite Tickets, attendee, purchaser, and order information are stored and managed by Eventbrite.'=>'When purchasing Eventbrite Tickets, attendee, purchaser, and order information are stored and managed by Eventbrite.','Please note that to create new events through the Community Events submission form, a user must hold a website account on this domain. This information is retained in the local database. It is also possible to create events anonymously, if the site owner has this option enabled.'=>'Please note that to create new events through the Community Events submission form, a user must hold a website account on this domain. This information is retained in the local database. It is also possible to create events anonymously, if the site owner has this option enabled.','Eventbrite Ticket information: name, description, cost, type, quantity'=>'Eventbrite Ticket information: name, description, cost, type, quantity','Import origin data (URL from where events are being imported—such as Eventbrite, MeetUp, other compatible URL sources, and more, which can include similar or same data as listed above)'=>'Import origin data (URL from where events are being imported—such as Eventbrite, MeetUp, other compatible URL sources, and more, which can include similar or same data as listed above)','Event information: website, cost, description, date, time, image'=>'Event information: website, cost, description, date, time, image','Venue information: name, address, city, country, state, postal code, phone, website, geographical coordinates (latitude and longitude)'=>'Venue information: name, address, city, country, province, postal code, phone, website, geographical coordinates (latitude and longitude)','Suggested text:'=>'Suggested text:','Through the usage of The Events Calendar, Events Calendar PRO, The Events Calendar Filter Bar, Eventbrite Tickets, and Community Events plugins, as well as our Event Aggregator Import service (contained within The Events Calendar plugin), information may be collected and stored within your website’s database.'=>'Through the usage of The Events Calendar, Events Calendar PRO, The Events Calendar Filter Bar, Eventbrite Tickets, and Community Events plugins, as well as our Event Aggregator Import service (contained within The Events Calendar plugin), information may be collected and stored within your website’s database.','All data present within a CSV or ICS file and external URLs (for events, venues, organizers, and tickets)'=>'All data present within a CSV or ICS file and external URLs (for events, venues, organisers, and tickets)','Importing Events, Venues, and Organizers:'=>'Importing Events, Venues, and Organisers:','Organizer information: name, phone, website, email'=>'Organiser information: name, phone, website, email','If you create, submit, import, save, or publish Event, Venue, or Organizer information, such information is retained in the local database:'=>'If you create, submit, import, save, or publish Event, Venue, or Organiser information, such information is retained in the local database:','What personal data we collect and why we collect it'=>'What personal data we collect and why we collect it','This information is only for guidance and not to be considered as legal advice.'=>'This information is only for guidance and not to be considered as legal advice.','Disclaimer:'=>'Disclaimer:','You should include the information below in the correct sections of you privacy policy.'=>'You should include the information below in the correct sections of you privacy policy.','This information serves as a guide on what sections need to be modified due to usage of The Events Calendar and its Add-ons.'=>'This information serves as a guide on what sections need to be modified due to usage of The Events Calendar and its Add-ons.','Hello,'=>'Hello,','The default event category for events imported via Eventbrite'=>'The default event category for events imported via Eventbrite','The default post status for events imported via Eventbrite'=>'The default post status for events imported via Eventbrite','Eventbrite Import Settings'=>'Eventbrite Import Settings','None'=>'None','Import from Eventbrite'=>'Import from Eventbrite','Learn more'=>'Learn more','Do more with Eventbrite Tickets'=>'Do more with Eventbrite Tickets','An event having a post meta value of `%s` minutes is not valid. Make sure it is from 0 to 59.'=>'An event having a post meta value of `%s` minutes is not valid. Make sure it is from 0 to 59.','An event having a post meta value of `%s` hour (24-hour) is not valid. Make sure it is from 0 to 23.'=>'An event having a post meta value of `%s` hour (24-hour) is not valid. Make sure it is from 0 to 23.','An event having a post meta value of `%s` hour (12-hour) is not valid. Make sure it is from 1 to 12.'=>'An event having a post meta value of `%s` hour (12-hour) is not valid. Make sure it is from 1 to 12.','An event having a post meta value of `%s` hour (am/pm) is not valid. Make sure it is from 1 to 12.'=>'An event having a post meta value of `%s` hour (am/pm) is not valid. Make sure it is from 1 to 12.','An event having a post meta value of `%s` meridian is not valid. Make sure it is either `am` or `pm`, or remove it entirely if using the 24-hour format.'=>'An event